[s0l0!-header][h1]Functions with Array Parameters[/h1][/s0l0!-header] 

An array cannot be passed by value to a function. However, an array name is a pointer, so just passing an array name to a function is passing a pointer to the array.

[s0l0!-header][b]Consider the following program:[/b][/s0l0!-header] [code format="c" codeId="1712"]int add_up ([b]int *a[/b], int num_elements);

int main() {
  int orders[5] = {100, 220, 37, 16, 98};

  printf("Total orders is %d\n", add_up(orders, 5)); 

  return 0;
}

int add_up ([b]int *a[/b], int num_elements) {
  int total = 0;
  int k;

  for (k = 0; k < num_elements; k++) {
    total += a[k];
  }

  return (total);
} [/code]
Program output is: "Total orders is 471"
[note]Run the code and see how it works![/note]

